{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Woe</b> — He speaks of Nebuchadnezzar, and his companion is the king of all the nations that he conquered." "The meaning of <b>משקה</b> is by way of parable: he made the nations drink the cup of poison." "<b>ומספח</b> — from the root of ספחני נא. The meaning is that you join kings to make them drink your fury, like the heat of water, and also intoxicate them so that their shame may be seen." "<b>מעוריהם</b> — like כמער איש. And the one who explains it of Belshazzar's feast, it is fitting, for one who looks there [profanes] HaShem, and so one must not say against HaShem. [n: The final clause וכן לא יאמר כנגד השם is obscure; translated hyper-literally. The phrase may be corrupt or elliptical.]"], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:54.096787233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}